abstract: >-
  Audit code, corrective patches and frozen numerical evidence for a
  leakage-safe reusability assessment of Squidiff, a diffusion model for
  single-cell development and perturbation prediction. Includes three
  regression-tested patches to the label-conditional interface, temporal
  splitting and training-window-only baselines, distribution, dependence and
  population-composition metrics, and the per-seed evaluation records at three
  leakage-safe temporal cutoffs with their same-distribution reference.
keywords:
  - reusability
  - reproducibility
  - single-cell transcriptomics
  - diffusion models
  - evaluation
  - data leakage
